{"benchmark": "ifeval", "task_id": "1082", "sample_idx": 4, "model_name": "google/gemma-3n-e4b-it", "content": "Arthur blinked, the morning sun feeling strangely… pixelated. He sat up in bed, the familiar floral wallpaper of his bedroom rendered with an unsettling sharpness, each tiny detail unnervingly perfect. A notification box, shimmering with a translucent glow, hovered in his vision: \"Welcome, Arthur! You have entered Aethelgard: Realm of Eldoria. Level 1 achieved. Quest: Retrieve the Sunstone.\" He rubbed his eyes, convinced he was still dreaming, but the notification remained. His reflection in the dresser mirror wasn't quite right either; his hair was a shade too golden, his eyes a bit too vibrant. He reached out to touch the wooden surface of the dresser, and instead of the expected grain, he felt a smooth, almost artificial texture. Panic began to bubble in his chest. This wasn't a dream. This was…real, yet impossibly unreal.\n\n***\n\nHe stumbled out of his room, finding his house eerily silent. The familiar scent of his mother’s baking was replaced by a faint, metallic tang. Peeking through the window, he saw his street transformed. The mundane suburban landscape had morphed into a quaint village square, complete with cobblestone streets and thatched-roof cottages. Villagers, dressed in medieval garb, bustled about, their movements jerky and slightly repetitive. A quest marker, a glowing icon of a sun, appeared above the village elder's head. Arthur stared, dumbfounded. He was trapped inside a video game, a character in someone else's meticulously crafted world. The Sunstone. He had a quest. He had to retrieve it. And somehow, he had to figure out how to get back home.\n\n\n\n", "logprobs": [{"token": "Arthur", "logprob": -0.16696929931640625}, {"token": "▁blinked", "logprob": -0.4622840881347656}, {"token": ",", "logprob": -0.0001805857609724626}, {"token": "▁the", "logprob": -0.06213567033410072}, {"token": "▁morning", "logprob": -1.015886902809143},